==Finnish==
{{Finnish index|p|e}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|fi|fiu-fin-pro|*pereh}}. Believed to come from the same [[Proto-Uralic]] root as {{m|fi|perä||rear}}, referring to the background of a person, compare {{m|fi|alkuperä||origin}}, {{m|fi|peräisin||originating from}}. First written appearance is from 1548 in the Finnish version of Sweden's {{m|fi|maanlaki||law of the country}} translated by a cleric known as {{w|lang=fi|Herra Martti}}.

Cognate with Karelian {{m|krl|pereh}}, Estonian {{m|et|pere}}, Võro {{m|vro|pereh}}, Veps {{m|vep|pereh}}, Livonian {{m|liv|perē}}.

